  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This problem has subtasks. You will receive 303030 points for solving the K≤NK \\leq NK≤N case.**\n\nYou're given an array AAA containing NNN integers.\n\nYou must perform the following operation **exactly** KKK times:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), and multiply AiA_iAi​ by 222.\n\nThat is, replace AiA_iAi​ with 2⋅Ai2\\cdot A_i2⋅Ai​.\nFind the minimum possible sum of the array AAA after all KKK operations have been performed.\n\nThis sum can be quite large, so print it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of the array and the number of operations to be performed.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the initial elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible final sum, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "0≤K≤1090 \\leq K \\leq 10^90≤K≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (30 points):** 0≤K≤N0 \\leq K \\leq N0≤K≤N.",
      "**Subtask 2 (70 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 2\n1 3 9 27\n5 0\n4 10 93 143 66\n2 2\n1000000000 500000004",
        "output": "43\n316\n999999994",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: It's optimal to use both moves to multiply A1A_1A1​ by 222, resulting in the array [4,3,9,27][4, 3, 9, 27][4,3,9,27]. The sum of this array is 434343.\nTest case 222: We have no moves, so just output the sum of the array.\nTest case 333: It's optimal to use one move each on both A1A_1A1​ and A2A_2A2​.\nThe resulting array is [2000000000,1000000008][2000000000, 1000000008][2000000000,1000000008], with a sum of 300000000830000000083000000008.\nModulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7, this is 999999994999999994999999994.\n\nThe next test can appear only in subtask 222."
      },
